1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:06,032
18xx Tiles is a reference for the track tiles in 18xx games.

2
00:00:06,032 --> 00:00:09,769
Every tile, from every game, in one place.

3
00:00:11,286 --> 00:00:15,930
It covers a large and growing library of 18xx games.

4
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:23,869
Each one shows its designer, its publisher, how many tiles come in the box, and a strip showing its mix of tile colors.

5
00:00:25,382 --> 00:00:33,178
Pick a game, and you see every tile it uses, drawn cleanly in its own color, with how many of each come in the box.

6
00:00:33,178 --> 00:00:38,683
You can filter by color, by cities or towns, or look up a tile by its number.

7
00:00:40,198 --> 00:00:46,810
Open any tile to see the full drawing, and every game that uses it, with the count in each box.

8
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:51,252
Tile fifty-seven, for example, turns up in many games.

9
00:00:52,758 --> 00:00:58,705
The common tiles page shows the standard tiles that game after game shares, all in one view.

10
00:01:00,206 --> 00:01:04,199
Sign in, and you can print tile-number stickers for your tile trays.

11
00:01:04,199 --> 00:01:09,797
Pick a game, choose the sticker size, and download a sheet that's ready for round labels.

12
00:01:11,302 --> 00:01:12,901
Spot a tile that's missing?

13
00:01:12,901 --> 00:01:13,845
Submit it.

14
00:01:13,845 --> 00:01:18,885
Every suggestion is reviewed before it's published, so the reference stays accurate.

15
00:01:20,406 --> 00:01:22,071
18xx Tiles.

16
00:01:22,071 --> 00:01:25,609
Every track tile, every game, one place.

